{% comment %}
  Footer: INFORMATION + CATEGORIES extras for Carbon.

  Preferred — Shopify Admin: Online store → Navigation. Open the menu assigned to each footer column
  (theme-specific names; often separate menus for “Information” / “Categories”).
  - INFORMATION: Add “Accessibility statement” → link to your Accessibility page (e.g. /pages/accessibility).
  - CATEGORIES: Add “JEANS” → same destination as the header mega menu Jeans hub. On shopcarbon.com that
    collection handle is `clothing-jeans` (URL /collections/clothing-jeans). If your mega menu differs, match it here.

  Theme code — inside each column’s `<ul>` (same pattern as existing `<li>` links), add:
    {% render 'carbon-footer-nav-additions', which: 'accessibility' %}
    {% render 'carbon-footer-nav-additions', which: 'jeans' %}
{% endcomment %}

{% liquid
  assign w = which | default: ''
%}

{% if w == 'accessibility' and pages.accessibility != blank %}
  <li>
    <a href="{{ pages.accessibility.url }}">Accessibility statement</a>
  </li>
{% elsif w == 'jeans' %}
  {% assign jeans_collection = collections['clothing-jeans'] %}
  {% if jeans_collection != blank %}
    <li>
      <a href="{{ jeans_collection.url }}">JEANS</a>
    </li>
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}
